First Missing Positive – for vs while (Revision Notes)
🧠 Problem Context

First Missing Positive problem me hume array ko in-place rearrange karna hota hai taaki
number x → index x-1 par ho.

🔑 Key Observation

Swap ke baad same index par naya element aata hai

Naya element bhi valid ho sakta hai (1 to n)

Ek index par multiple swaps possible hote hain

❓ while loop kyun use hota hai?

while loop ka use tab hota hai jab ek index ko tab tak process karna ho jab tak wo completely correct na ho jaye.

Conditions:
while(nums[i] > 0 && nums[i] <= n && nums[i] != nums[nums[i]-1])

Reason:

Swap ke baad nums[i] change ho jata hai

Same index par aaya hua element bhi correct position chahta hai

Isliye re-check zaroori hota hai

❌ if kyun sufficient nahi hai?

if sirf ek baar check karta hai

Swap ke baad index ka kaam incomplete reh sakta hai

for loop aage badh jata hai aur index fully fix nahi hota

🧠 External for loop ka role

for loop array ke har index par jaane ke liye hota hai

Ensures every index is visited

Index traversal ka kaam karta hai

Index ko fix nahi karta

🧠 Internal while loop ka role

while loop current index ko completely fix karta hai

Same index par multiple swaps allow karta hai

Jab tak element sahi jagah par na aa jaye, loop nahi rukta

🔁 for vs while (Clear Difference)
Loop	Purpose
for	Har index par visit karna
while	Same index ko sahi position tak fix karna
🧩 Decision Rule (Very Important)

Agar swap ke baad SAME index par naya element aata hai
aur usse bhi process karna padta hai → while mandatory hai
